<nowiki>[[M. Jayachandran,alphones joseph.</nowiki>\nRajeev Alunkal (lyrics)\n|cinematography = Venugopalan\n|editing        = G. Murali\n|studio         =\n|distributor    =\n|released       = {{Film date|2007|10|18|df=y}}\n|runtime        =\n|country        = India\n|language       = Malayalam\n|budget         =\n|gross          =\n}}\n\u0022\u0022'Black Cat\u0022\u0022' is a 2007 Indian Malayalam action thriller film written and directed by [[Vinayan]] and starring [[Suresh Gopi]] and [[Meena Durairaj|Meena]].\n\n==Cast==\n*[[Suresh Gopi]]... Ramesh Sharma IPS (Commissioner of Police) and Black\n*[[Meena Durairaj]]\n*[[Karthika Mathew|Karthika]]...Blessy\n*[[Rajan P. Dev]]\n*[[Harisree Asokan]]\n*[[Abu Salim (actor)|Abu Salim]]\n*[[Ramu (actor)|Ramu]]\n*Geetha Nair as Ramesh Sharma's mother\n*[[Sajitha Betti]] as Ramesh Sharma's sister  \n*Dimple Rose Ramesh Sharma's younger sister\n\n==External links==\n*{{IMDb title|0997142|Black Cat}}\n*[https://web.archive.org/web/20120223211210/http://connect.in.com/black-cat-malayalam/profile-390415.html Black Cat (Malayalam)]\n\n[[Category:2007 films]]\n[[Category:
 Malayalam-language films]]\n[[Category:Indian films]]\n\n\n{{
-Malayalam-film-stub}}</text>\n      <sha1>ngkf8rrk0ijg72ndqx18gehyljcpfp1</sha1>\n    </revision>\n  </page>\n  <page>\n    <title>Danner Pachi</title>\n    <ns>0</ns>\n    <id>23546601</id>\n    <revision>\n      <id>775778936</id>\n      <parentid>762553568</parentid>\n      <timestamp>2017-04-17T01:51:36Z</timestamp>\n      <contributor>\n        <username>Red Director</username>\n        <id>1261736</id>\n      </contributor>\n      <minor />\n      <comment>v1.41 - minor cleanup</comment>\n      <model>wikitext</model>\n      <format>text/x-wiki</format>\n      <text xml:space=\u0022preserve\u0022>{{Infobox football biography\n| name = Danner Pachi\n| image = \n| fullname = Danner Jesús Pachi Bozo\n| height = {{height|m=1.66}}\n| birth_date  =  1984-04-01 }}\n| birth_place = [[Caranavi]], [[Bolivia]]\n| currentclub  = \n| clubnumber = \n| position = [[Midfielder (association football)|Midfielder]]\n| youthyears1 = \n| youthclubs1 = \n| years1 = 2001–2007  \n| years2 = 2007  \n| years3 = 2008  \n| years4 = 2009  \n| years5 = 2010  \n| years6 = 2010\n| years7 = 2011\n| years8 = 2011–2012 \n| years9 = 2014\n| clubs1 = [[Club Bolívar|Bolívar]]  \n| clubs2 = → [[Club Jorge Wilstermann|Wilstermann]] \u0022(loan)\u0022 \n| clubs3 = [[Club Bolívar|Bolívar]]  \n| clubs4 = [[Liga Deportiva Universitaria de Portoviejo|LDU Portoviejo]]  \n| clubs5 = [[Club Bolívar|Bolívar]]  \n| clubs6 = [[Club Deportivo ESPOLI|Espoli]]\n| clubs7 = [[Guabirá]]\n| clubs8 = [[Club Real Potosí|Real Potosí]]\n| clubs9 = [[Sport Boys Warnes]]\n| caps1 = 203   \n| caps2 = 19    \n| caps3 = 26    \n| caps4 = 24    \n| caps5 = 10   \n| caps6 = 15\n| caps7 = 19 \n| caps8 = 31\n| caps9 = 22\n| goals1 = 35  \n| goals2 = 3  \n| goals3 = 8  \n| goals4 = 7  \n| goals5 = 0 \n| goals6 = 1\n| goals7 = 2  \n| goals8 = 0\n| goals9 = 0\n| nationalyears1 = 2004–2009\n| nationalteam1 = [[Bolivia national football team|Bolivia]]\n| nationalcaps1 = 13  \n| nationalgoals1 = 0 \n| pcupdate = October 20, 2010\n| ntupdate = October 12, 2009\n}}\n\n\u0022'Danner Jesús Pachi Bozo\u0022' (born April 1, 1984 in [[Caranavi]]) is a [[Bolivia]]n football midfielder that is currently without a club.\n\n==Club career==\nPachi began his career in 2001 with Bolivian giant [[Club Bolívar|Bolívar]]. He spent nearly 7 years with the club with over 200 league appearances throughout this period. In the winter of 2007 he was loaned to [[Club Jorge Wilstermann|Wilstermann]], but after six months Bolívar claimed back his services. In his return to the \u0022academia\u0022, Pachi had an outstanding 2008 season. His good performance awoke the interest of many clubs abroad. In January 2009, he signed for Ecuadorian club [[Liga Deportiva Universitaria de Portoviejo|LDU Portoviejo]], which was relegated at the end of the season. The next year he returned to Bolívar, but did not get much playing time. In 2011, he signed for club [[Guabirá]].\n\n==International
