[Wales national under-16 rugby union team[Wales national under-20 rugby union team\n| ru_nationalcaps        = 4 \n| ru_nationalpoints      = (0)\n| ru_ntupdate            = 21 Jan 2014\n| ru_sevensnationalyears =  \n| ru_sevensnationalteam  = \n| ru_sevensnationalcomp  = \n| ru_coachyears          = \n| ru_coachclubs          = \n| ru_refereeyears        = \n| ru_refereecomps        = \n| ru_refereeapps         = \n}}\n\n\u0022'Sam Parry\u0022' (born 17 December 1991) is a Welsh rugby union player. His position is hooker.\n\nParry began his rugby career at [[Llandovery RFC]] before joining the [[Scarlets]] Under
 and then the Newport Gwent Dragons academy. He made his senior debut for Newport Gwent Dragons against [[Bath Rugby|Bath]] on 15 October 2011. Parry joined the [[Ospreys (rugby team)|Ospreys]] for the 2014-15 season.\n\n==International==\n\nIn May 2013 he was selected in the [[Wales national rugby union team]] training squad for the summer 2013 tour to Japan.\n\nIn January 2014 he was called up to the Wales squad for the [[2014 Six Nations Championship]].\n\n== References ==\n{{Reflist}}\n^ Ospreys splash\n\n== External links ==\n* [http://www.newportgwentdragons.com/Teams/Player/Dragons/144135 Newport Gwent Dragons profile] \nOspreys profile\n\n{{Ospreys squad}}\n\n{{DEFAULTSORT:Parry, Sam}}\n[[Category:People from Haverfordwest]]\n[[Category:Welsh rugby union players]]\n[[Category:Newport Gwent Dragons players]]\n[[Category:Newport RFC players]]\n[[Category:Living people]]\n[[Category:1991 births]]\n\n\n{{Wales-rugbyunion-bio-stub}}</text>\n      <sha1>lkxau9gabf0intc6lmgqprqhxbt43ki</sha1>\n    </revision>\n  </page>\n  <page>\n    <title>Category:Southwestern Athletic Conference football champion seasons</title>\n    <ns>14</ns>\n    <id>34318104</id>\n    <revision>\n      <id>470285643</id>\n      <timestamp>2012-01-08T17:19:38Z</timestamp>\n      <contributor>\n        <username>Bsuorangecrush</username>\n        <id>8014785</id>\n      </contributor>\n      <comment>Created page with 'This category comprises articles pertaining to football teams that won the [[Southwestern Athletic Conference]].  [[Category:Southwestern Athletic Conference foo...'</comment>\n      <model>wikitext</model>\n      <format>text/x-wiki</format>\n      <text xml:space=\u0022preserve\u0022>This category comprises articles pertaining to football teams that won the [[Southwestern Athletic Conference]].\n\n[[Category:Southwestern Athletic Conference football seasons|Champion]]\n[[Category:College football conference champion seasons]]</text>\n      <sha1>4yllqd96ziddtmw4dkvis2kcygsbgzx</sha1>\n    </revision>\n  </page>\n  <page>\n    <title>Buttar Bakhuha</title>\n    <ns>0</ns>\n    <id>34318114</id>\n    <revision>\n      <id>770270607</id>\n      <parentid>736078664</parentid>\n      <timestamp>2017-03-14T12:43:23Z</timestamp>\n      <contributor>\n        <username>JJMC89 bot</username>\n        <id>27446209</id>\n      </contributor>\n      <comment>Migrate {{Infobox settlement}} coordinates parameters to {{Coord}}, see [[Wikipedia:Coordinates in infoboxes]]</comment>\n      <model>wikitext</model>\n      <format>text/x-wiki</format>\n      <text xml:space=\u0022preserve\u0022>{{Use Indian English|date=August 2013}}\n{{Use dmy dates|date=August 2013}}\n{{Infobox settlement\n| name                    = Buttar Bakhuha\n| native_name             = ਬੁੱਟਰ ਬਖੂਹਾ\n| native_name_lang        = pa\n| other_name              = \n| nickname                = \n| settlement_type         = village\n| image_skyline           = \n| image_alt               = \n| image_caption           = \n| pushpin_map             = India Punjab#India\n| pushpin_label_position  = \n| pushpin_map_alt         = \n| pushpin_map_caption     = Location in Punjab, India\n| coordinates             = {{coord|30.438111|N|74.665725|E|display=inline,title}}\n| subdivision_type        = Country\n| s
