\n|capacity              = \n|dome_quantity         = 1\n|dome_height_outer     = \n|dome_dia_outer        = \n|minaret_quantity      =  \n|minaret_height        = \n}}\n\nThe \u0022'At-Taqwa Mosque\u0022' ({{zh|c=大園清真寺|p=Dàyuán Qīngzhēnsì}}) is a [[mosque]] in [[Dayuan District]], [[Taoyuan City]], [[Taiwan]]. It is the seventh and latest mosque built in Taiwan.\n\n==History==\nThe mosque development was started by an [[Indonesia]]n-Taiwanese couple who own an Indonesian shop around the area where most of the Indonesian workers work at the factories or in households. They purchased empty land beside their shop to build a mosque. With the help of funding and lending from various organizations, the mosque could finally be constructed a year later. The mosque was officially opened on 9 June 2013.\n\n==Activities==\nBeside hosting the normal [[Salat|five compulsory daily prayers]] for Muslims, the mosque also regularly holds classes, such as [[Standard Chinese|Mandarin language]].\n\n==Architecture==\n\n\nThis 130 square metre mosque is 
 in length and 
 in width. The building consists of three stories, in which the first story is dedicated for the male prayer hall, the second story is for the female prayer hall and guest room, and the third floor is for classes and dormitories.\n\n==Transportation==\nAt-Taqwa Mosque is accessible north west from [[Dayuan Station]] of the [[Taoyuan Metro]].\n\n==See also==\n* [[Islam in Taiwan]]\n* [[Chinese Muslim Association]]\n* [[Chinese Muslim Youth League]]\n* [[List of mosques in Taiwan]]\n* [[Indonesians in Taiwan]]\n\n==Referenc
