[[Munich]], Germany's Reich der Kristalle museum replica of the 
 [[Rundell and Bridge]] recut of the Nassak Diamond. In reality the diamond was nowhere near this blue, being a white Type IIa classic Golconda diamond. The term \u0022blue-white\u0022 is often used to describe these diamonds but in reality alongside a modern D-color diamond it would have had an extremely faint blue cast. Its cut was also more complex (see below images).
