|[Swansea_City_A.F.C.]]\n| most successful clubs = [[Reading FC| Reading]]\n[[Southampton FC|Southampton]]  (1)\n| website               =  }}\n\n\u0022'The Premier League Cup\u0022' is an [[England|English]] [[Association football|football]] competition run by [[Premier League]] for under–23 sides.\n\nThe competition was created in 2013 as the \u0022'U21 Premier League Cup\u0022' - an U21 equivalent of the [[FA Youth Cup]] (an U18 competition competed for since 1952), albeit being run by the Premier League instead of The [[The Football Association|FA]]. In 2016 the age range of the competition was raised to Under
, and the competition was renamed as simply the \u0022'Premier League Cup\u0022'.\n\n==Winners==\n===Finals===\n{| class=\u0022wikitable\u0022 \n|-\n! Year\n! Winners\n! Score\n! Runners-up\n! Note\n|-\n|[[2013–14 Under-21 Premier League Cup|2013-14]]\n|align=right| [[Reading F.C.| Reading]]\n|align=center|[[2013–14 Under-21 Premier League Cup#Final|4 – 3]]{{asterisk}}\n|align=left| [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]]\n|-\n|[[2014–15 Under-21 Premier League Cup|2014-15]]\n|align=right| [[Southampton F.C. Under
