{{Singles\n  | Name          = Mixed Up\n  | Type          =remix\n  | single 1      = [[Never Enough (The Cure song)|Never Enough]]\n  | single 1 date = September 17, 1990\n  | single 2      = [[Close to Me (The Cure song)|Close to Me (remix)]]\n  | single 2 date = October 22, 1990\n  | single 3      = [[A Forest|A Forest (Tree Mix)]]\n  | single 3 date = December 6, 1990\n  }}\n}}\n{{Album reviews\n|rev1 = [[AllMusic]]\n|rev1score = {{Rating|2|5}}\n|rev2 = \u0022[[Entertainment Weekly]]\u0022\n|rev2score = C\n|rev3 = \u0022[[The Rolling Stone Album Guide]]\u0022\n|rev3score = {{Rating|1|5}}\n|rev4 = \u0022[[Stylus Magazine]]\u0022\n|rev4score = (positive)\n}}\n\n\u0022\u0022'Mixed Up\u0022\u0022' is a 1990 remix album by British [[alternative rock]] band [[The Cure]]. The songs are remixes of some of their hits, reflecting the popularity of remixing of existing songs and dance culture of the late 
 and early 
.\n\nMost of the songs are extended mixes. Several had been previously released on [[12\u0022]] singles, but some are completely remade, with Smith recutting vocals due to the original tapes not being available. The record closes with the extended version of a new single, \u0022[[Never Enough (The Cure song)|Never Enough]]\u0022. The remix of \u0022Pictures of You\u0022 was originally released under the title \u0022(Strange Mix)\u0022.  In an interview featured on the [[The Cure: Trilogy|\u0022Trilogy\u0022 DVD]], singer Robert Smith described the [[remix album]] as something \u0022fun after the doom and gloom of \u0022[[Disintegration (The Cure album)|Disintegration]]\u0022\u0022.\n\nThe Cure also released some other new mixes as the b-sides of the singles from Mixed Up: the first single, \u0022Never Enough\u0022, featured a remix of \u0022Let's Go To Bed\u0022, entitled \u0022Let's Go To Bed (Milk Mix)\u0022 (on the 12\u0022, cassette and CD versions), as well as a new song, \u0022Harold and Joe\u0022, while the second single, \u0022Close to Me (Remix)\u0022 contained \u0022Just Like Heaven (Dizzy Mix)\u0022 (on all formats) and \u0022Primary (Red Mix)\u0022 (on the 12\u0022, CD and cassette versions) as b-sides, the third single, \u0022A Forest (Tree Mix)\u0022 contained the original version of the song and \u0022Inbetween Days (Shiver Mix)\u0022 (only on 5inch CD) as b-sides.\n\n==Track listing==\n\n===LP edition===\n{{tracklist\n| headline        = Side A\n| title1          = [[Lullaby (The Cure song)|Lullaby]] (Extended Mix) \n| length1         = 7:43\n| title2          = [[Close to Me (The Cure song)|Close to Me]] (Closer Mix)\n| length2         = 5:44\n| title3          = [[Fascination Street]] (Extended Mix)\n| length3         = 8:47\n}}\n\n{{tracklist\n| headline        = Side B\n| title4          = [[The Walk (The Cure song)|The Walk]] (Everything Mix)\n| length4         = 5:27\n| title5          = [[Lovesong (The Cur
