<nowiki>[[konkuduru], </nowiki>[[East Godavari District]], [[Andhra Pradesh]]\n| residence     = [[Hyderabad, India|Hyderabad]], Telangana , India\n| occupation    = Film Director, Screen-play writer, Story writer and Dialogue writer, Song write, Producer\n| alias     = Director Chandu\n}}\n\n\u0022'Chandu\u0022' (born \u0022'Satti Chandra Sekhar Reddy\u0022', 17 October 1975) is an [[Indian people|Indian]] film director, producer, and screenwriter who predominantly worked in [[Telugu cinema]]. Born in konkuduru near [[Kakinada]], [[East Godavari district]] of [[Andhra Pradesh]], He studied at St.anns and S.K.V.T. high school in Rajahmundry.\n\n==Career==\nChandu has started his career as an Assistant Director for the movie  [[Kalyana Ramudu]]  which was directed by \u0022Chirunavvutho Ramprasad\u0022 and [[Samba (2004 film)]] directed by [[V. V. Vinayak]]. In 2005 Producer Shyam prasad  has given first direction opportunity to Chandu, in [[SP Entertainments]] for [[10th Class]] movie, It was released and declared as a Hit in 2006, Later in 2007 his second Directorial Venture Note Book He launch a star kid Rajeev(son of [[Saluri Koteswara Rao]] \u0022Koti\u0022 Music director). In 2013 Chandu wrote and Directed [[Prema Oka Maikam]] under Touring Talkies produced by NRI Mr D.venkata suresh and K.Surya Srikanth.\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:1975 births]]\n[[Category:Living people]]\n[[Category:Indian film directors]]</text>\n      <sha1>6pygxuja0xyaz6xfqpy7fxyudmtk9fz</sha1>\n    </revision>\n  </page>\n  <page>\n    <title>Wikipedia:Textwall</title>\n    <ns>4</ns>\n    <id>49882343</id>\n    <redirect title=\u0022Wikipedia:Wall of text\u0022 />\n    <revision>\n      <id>711174521</id>\n      <parentid>711174475</parentid>\n      <timestamp>2016-03-21T08:53:58Z</timestamp>\n      <contributor>\n        <username>SMcCandlish</username>\n        <id>378390</id>\n      </contributor>\n      <comment>rcat</comment>\n      <model>wikitext</model>\n      <format>text/x-wiki</format>\n      <text xml:space=\u0022preserve\u0022>#REDIRECT [[Wikipedia:Wall of text]]\n{{R from modification}}</text>\n      <sha1>3j82pwawrmzkxb1vhndqycjj67r6a
</sha1>\n    </revision>\n  </page>\n  <page>\n    <title>List of Lip Sync Battle Philippines episodes</title>\n    <ns>0</ns>\n    <id>49882344</id>\n    <revision>\n      <id>778562763</id>\n      <parentid>778553599</parentid>\n      <timestamp>2017-05-03T22:11:24Z</timestamp>\n      <contributor>\n        <username>Oripaypaykim</username>\n        <id>23820005</id>\n      </contributor>\n      <minor />\n      <comment>Reverted 1 edit by [[Special:Contributions/130.105.230.101|130.105.230.101]] ([[User talk:130.105.230.101|talk]]) to last revision by Oripaypaykim. ()</comment>\n      <model>wikitext</model>\n      <format>text/x-wiki</format>\n      <text xml:space=\u0022preserve\u0022>\u0022\u0022'[[Lip Sync Battle Philippines]]\u0022\u0022' is a Philippine [[music]]al-[[reality competition]] television series broadcast by [[GMA Network]]. Hosted by [[Michael V.]] and [[Iya Villania]], the show premiered on February 27, 2016 succeeding \u0022[[Celebrity Bluff]]\u0022. It is the Philippine version of the American reality television series [[Lip Sync Battle|under the same title]].\n\n==Series overview==\n<onlyinclude>\n{| class=\u0022wikitable plainrowheaders\u0022  style=\u0022text-align:center;\u0022\n|-\n! scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022padding:0 8px;\u0022 colspan=\u00222\u0022 rowspan=\u00222\u0022| Season\n! scope=\u0022col\u0022 style=\u0022padding:0 8px;\u0022 rowspan=\u00222\u0022| Episodes\n!
