circa-1947\n|birth_place=[[Lakeba]], [[Lau Islands]], Fiji\n|death_date=\n|death_place=\n|style=[[Orthodox stance|Orthodox]]\n|total=40\n|wins=24 ([[Knockout|KO]] 11)\n|losses=15 (KO 5)\n|draws=1\n|no contests=\n|medaltemplates=\n}}\n\u0022'Alipate \u0022Al\u0022 Korovou\u0022' born in [[Lakeba]], [[Lau Islands]] is a [[Fijians|Fijian]] [[professional]] [[middleweight|middle]]/[[super middleweight]] [[Boxing|boxer]] of the 
 who won the New South Wales (Australia) State middleweight title, [[List of Australian middleweight boxing champions|Australian middleweight title]], Australian super middleweight title, and [[List of Commonwealth Boxing Council Champions#Middleweight|Commonwealth middleweight title]], his professional fighting weight varied from {{convert|156+1/2|lb|kg stlb||abbr=on}}, i.e. [[middleweight]] to  166 lb , i.e. [[super middleweight]].\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n==External links==\n*{{Boxrec|id=44554}}\n*[http://static.boxrec.com/b/b5/Al_Korovou.jpg Image - Al Korovou]\n*[http://www.sportingpulse.com/assoc_page.cgi?client=1-3653-0-0-0&sID=35815&&news_task=DETAIL&articleID=599407 Article - Al Korovou]\n\n{{DEFAULTSORT:Korovou, Al}}\n[[Category:People from Lakeba]]\n[[Category:Living people]]\n[[Category:Middleweight boxers]]\n[[Category:Super-middleweight boxers]]\n[[Category:Year of birth missing (living people)]]\n[[Category:Fijian male boxers]]\n[[Category:I-Taukei Fijian people]]\n\n\n{{Fiji-boxing-bio-stub}}</text>\n      <sha1>sjzoprqxyvyly5bj01mpdezb9syang8</sha1>\n    </revision>\n  </page>\n  <page>\n    <title>Strict snake eel</title>\n    <ns>0</ns>\n    <id>40626346</id>\n    <revision>\n      <id>742963363</id>\n      <parentid>634360411</parentid>\n      <timestamp>2016-10-06T22:39:41Z</timestamp>\n      <contributor>\n        <username>Murmeldjuret</username>\n        <id>24253262</id>\n      </contributor>\n      <comment>image</comment>\n      <model>wikitext</model>\n      <format>text/x-wiki</format>\n      <text xml:space=\u0022preserve\u0022>{{Taxobox\n| image = FMIB 51813 Xyrias revulsus Jordan & Snyder Family Ophichthyidae Misaki, Japan.jpeg\n| regnum = [[Animalia]]\n| phylum = [[Chordata]]\n| classis = [[Actinopterygii]]\n| ordo = [[Anguilliformes]]\n| familia = [[Ophichthidae]]\n| genus = \u0022[[Xyrias]]\u0022\n| species = \u0022\u0022'X. revulsus\u0022\u0022'\n| binomial = \u0022Xyrias revulsus\u0022\n| binomial_authority = Jordan & Snyder, 1901 \n| synonyms_ref = \n| synonyms = \n}}\nThe \u0022'Strict snake eel\u0022' (\u0022\u0022'Xyrias revulsus\u0022\u0022') is an [[eel]] in the family [[Ophichthidae]] (worm/snake eels). It was described by [[David Starr Jordan]] and [[John Otterbein Snyder]] in 1901. It is a [[marine biology|marine]], [[temperate]] water-dwelling eel which is known from the Indo-Pacific, including [[Japan]], the [[Philippines]], the [[China Sea]], and [[South Africa]]. It dwells at a depth range of  146 to . Males can reach a maximum [[total length]] of  
 .\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Ophichthidae]]\n[[Category:Animals described in 1901]]\n\n{{Anguilliformes-stub}}</text>\n      <sha1>nwsbh7icghhdkwa1jbsrojqaqbzuck8</sha1>\n    </revision>\n  </page>\n  <page>\n    <title>Xyrias revulsus</title>\n    <ns>0</ns>\n    <id>40626347</id>\n    <redirect title=\u0022Strict snake eel\u0022 />\n    <revision>\n      <id>574440041</id>\n      <timesta
