\u0022N\u0022,\u0022N′\u0022-(1,4-Piperazinediyldi-3,1-propanediyl)bis[2-amino-5-[(aminoiminomethyl)amino]-, (2\u0022S\u0022,2\u0022S\u0022)-pentanamide\n| image = Ciraparantag.svg\n| alt =\n| caption =\n\n\n| pronounce =\n| tradename =\n| Drugs.com =\n| MedlinePlus =\n| pregnancy_AU = \n| pregnancy_AU_comment =\n| pregnancy_US = \n| pregnancy_category =\n| legal_AU = \n| legal_AU_comment =\n| legal_CA = \n| legal_DE = \n| legal_NZ = \n| legal_UK = \n| legal_US = \n| legal_UN = \n| legal_status = Investigational\n| routes_of_administration = [[Intravenous]]\n\n\n| bioavailability =\n| protein_bound =\n| metabolism =\n| metabolites =\n| onset = 
\n| elimination_half-life =\n| duration_of_action = 24 hours\n| excretion =\n\n\n| CAS_number = 1438492-26-2\n| ATCvet =\n| ATC_prefix = None\n| ATC_suffix =\n| PubChem = 71576543\n| DrugBank =\n| ChemSpiderID = 33427375\n| UNII = U2R67KV65Q\n| KEGG_Ref = {{keggcite|correct|kegg}}\n| KEGG = D10868\n| synonyms = PER977\n\n\n\n| C=22 | H=48 | N=12 | O=2\n| molecular_weight  =\n| smiles = C1CN(CCN1CCCNC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(=N)N)N)CCCNC(=O)[C@H](CCCNC(=N)N)N\n| StdInChI=
/C22H48N12O2/c23-17(5-1-7-31-21(25)26)19(35)29-9-3-11-33-13-15-34(16-14-33)12-4-10-30-20(36)18(24)6-2-8-32-22(27)28/h17
,1-16,23-24H2,(H,29,35)(H,30,36)(H4,25,26,31)(H4,27,28,32)/t17-,18-/m0/s1\n| StdInChIKey = HRDUUSCYRPOMSO-ROUUACIJSA-N\n}}\n\n\u0022'Ciraparantag\u0022' ([[International Nonproprietary Name|INN]]/[[United States Adopted Name|USAN]], or \u0022'aripazine\u0022') is a drug under investigation as an [[antidote]] for a number of [[anticoagulant]] (anti-blood clotting) drugs, including [[Direct Xa inhibitor|factor Xa inhibitor]]s ([[rivaroxaban]], [[apixaban]] and [[edoxaban]]), [[dabigatran]], [[low molecular weight heparin]]s and [[unfractionated heparin]].\n\n==Mechanism of action==\nAccording to \u0022[[in vitro]]\u0022 studies, the substance binds directly to anticoagulants via [[hydrogen bond]]s from or to various parts of the molecule:\n{| class=\u0022wikitable\u0022\n|-\n! Hydrogen bonds\n! Rivaroxaban\n! Apixaban\n! Edoxaban\n! Dabigatran\n! Heparins\n|-\n| [[Guanidine]] part\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| \n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n|-\n| α-Amino group\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| \n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n|-\n| [[Amide]] nitrogen\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| \n| \n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n|-\n| Amide oxygen\n| \n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| {{Check mark|15}}\n| \n| \n|}\n\n==Chemical properties==\nCiraparantag consists of two -[[arginine]] units connected with a [[piperazine]] containing linker chain.\n\n==See also==\n\n===Other anticoagulant antidotes===\n* [[Andexanet alfa]]\n* [[Idarucizumab]]\n* [[Vitamin K]]\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Amino acid derivatives]]
