*Main guns: 3 × [[3\u0022/50 caliber gun|3 inch /50]] Mk 22 dual purpose open mount, and fixed fire shot (anti-aircraft, armor-piercing, or starshell) and had a range of  14600 yd  at 45 degrees, and an anti-aircraft ceiling of  28000 ft \n*[[Anti-aircraft]] guns: 4 × [[1.1 inch/75 (
) gun|1.1 inch]] or 2 × [[Bofors 
 gun|
 Bofors]] guns were fitted in the 'X' position on the \u0022Buckley\u0022-Class units; these were not included in the Captain-Class units. 8 × [[Oerlikon 
 cannon|
 Oerlikon]] single-mount cannon positioned two in front of the bridge behind and above B gun mount, one each side of B gun mount in sponsons, and two each side of the ship in sponsons just abaft the funnel. Some of the ships had an extra one or two Oerlikons fitted on top of the superstructure amidships. The Captain-Class units had additional 
 guns fitted in 'X' position, and on the director stand for 'X' position.\n*[[Torpedo tube]]s: 3 [[Mark 15 torpedo| 21 in ]] torpedo tubes in a triple mount were mounted just aft of the stack.\n*[[Hedgehog (weapon)|Hedgehog]]: British designed ahead throwing mortar which fired 24 bombs ahead of the ship, this was situated on the main deck just aft of A gun mount.\n*[[Depth charge]]s: Up to 200 were carried. Two sets of double rails each side of the ship at the stern, each set held 24 charges; eight (two on Captain-class units) [[K-gun]] depth charge throwers each holding 5 charges, were situated each side of the ship just forward of the stern rails. On Captain-Class ships, just forward of these double sets of ready racks were fitted along each side of the ship extending to midships, each set holding 60 depth charges (these ready rails were added after the ships first arrived in the UK)
