(1) Norman led the move to establish a municipally-owned power plant in his small city of [[Minden, Louisiana|Minden]], rather than reliance on a private company supplying [[electricity]].\n\n(2) Norman became one of the first [[Democratic Party (United States)|Democrats]] in [[Louisiana]] to be unseated by a [[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]], as the two-party system slowly began to emerge in the 
.\n\n(3) Norman was particularly active in the [[Masonic lodge]] and the [[Baptist]] Church.\n\n(4) Norman became the first student to enroll at the Ringling School of Art in [[Sarasota, Florida]], where he studied under [[Ben Earl Looney]], a Minden native.
