{{bda|1997|6|10}}\n| birth_place = [[Australia]]\n| height = \n| position = [[Midfielder]]\n| currentclub  = [[Brisbane Roar FC (W-League)|Brisbane Roar]]\n| clubnumber  = 7\n| youthyears1= \n| youthclubs1=\n| years1= 2013–2015\n| clubs1= [[Brisbane Roar FC (W-League)|Brisbane Roar]]\n| caps1= 13 | goals1 = 2\n| years2= 2015–2016\n| clubs2= [[Sydney FC (W-League)|Sydney FC]]\n| caps2= 12 | goals2 = 0\n| years3= 2016–\n| clubs3= [[Brisbane Roar FC (W-League)|Brisbane Roar]]\n| caps3= 6 | goals3 = 0\n| nationalyears1=     | nationalteam1=Australia U-17 | nationalcaps1= 8| nationalgoals1 = 9\n| nationalyears2=2014–| nationalteam2=Australia U-19 | nationalcaps2= 3 | nationalgoals2 = 7\n| pcupdate = 13 February 2017\n| ntupdate =\n}}\n\n\u0022'Sunny Kathleen Franco\u0022' (born 10 June 1997) is an [[Australian]] [[football (soccer)]] player who plays for [[Brisbane Roar FC (W-League)|Brisbane Roar]] in the Australian [[W-League (Australia)|W-League]].\n\n==Overview==\n[[Queensland Australian Football League|Queensland]] is known to have been producing players of calibre for the [[Australia women's national soccer team|Matildas]], from Sue Monteath to current captain, [[Clare Polkinghorne]]. Sunny Franco has retained this legacy as Matildas captain under the U17 contingent.\n\nWhile the team is gearing up for the AFC U
 Girls Championships, Franco is headed for doubling as a World Cup qualifier and a major contender to represent Australia. The sixteen year player has fortified her position within the past year by producing remarkable goal scores in the Championship qualifiers last November in [[Manila]]. A month later she scored six goals in the [[2015 AFC U-19 Women's Championship qualification#Group C|AFC U-19 qualifier]] for Australia.\n\nIn October 2016, Franco returned to [[Brisbane Roar FC (W-League)|Brisbane Roar]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://thewomensgame.com/2016/10/brisbane-roar-release-full-squad-for-season-9/|title=Brisbane Roar release squad members f
