[[Indian Standard Time|local\n| utc_offset1             = +5:43\n| postal_code_type        = \n| postal_code             = 442908\n| registration_plate      = \n| website                 = \n| footnotes               = \n}}\n\n\u0022'Gadchandur\u0022' ( \u0022गडचांदुर\u0022 ) is a city and [[Municipal Council]] in [[Chandrapur district]], [[Maharashtra]], [[India]].\u0022'Gadchandur\u0022' is named after the fort Chandur.Gadchandur has some tourist places \n1) Lord Shiva temple\n2) Lord Vishnu temple\n3) Manikgarh fort\nGadchandur is famous because of the Manikgarh cement Factory\n\n==Villages near Gadchandur==\n\n*Thutra (
