8 October 2010\n|  Genre       = [[Electro music|Electro]], [[Electronic body music|EBM]], [[Industrial music|Industrial]]\n|  Length      = \n|  Label       = [[L-Tracks Recordings]]\n|  Producer    = [[Faderhead]]\n|  Last album  = \u0022[[Faderhead Trilogy|Trilogy]]\u0022\n(2009)\n|  This album  = \u0022Black Friday\u0022\n(2010)\n|  Next album  = \u0022[[The World of Faderhead]]\u0022\n(2012) \n| Misc =\n{{ Singles\n  | Name           = Black Friday\n  | Type           = Studio album\n  | Single 1       = Destroy Improve Rebuild\n  | Single 1 date  = 2010\n  | Single 2       = The Way to Fuck God\n  | Single 2 date  = 11 November 2011\n}}\n}}\n{{Album ratings\n| rev1 = [[COMA Music Magazine]]\n| rev1Score = (Favorable)\n}}\n\u0022\u0022'Black Friday\u0022\u0022' is [[Faderhead]]'s fourth [[album]]. It was released 8 October 2010. It is the first album title not to follow the FH album trend, as unlike previous albums, Black Friday is Faderhead's first [[concept album]]. There are 16 tracks, each a new part of the overall [[story arc]]. It tells the story of a Friday night gone wrong, from the end of the working day, to the fun in the clubs, the inevitable crash, and all the chaos in between. A short film has been shot to tie in with the promotion of the album, and portrays the story in a visual medium.\n\n\u0022Destroy Improve Rebuild\u0022 is set to be the first single for the album. It has already been previewed at various gigs in 2010, and Faderhead has released a Club Edit as well as for the tracks \u0022Do You Know Who I Think I Am?\u0022 and \u0022The Way to Fuck God\u0022.\n\nThe 15-minute short film for Black Friday was released on the official website in November 2010.\n\nIn 2011 saw the release of 'The Way to Fuck Clubs' EP. It featured remixes and a live acoustic, as well as a new demo when purchased through the Faderhead website.\n\n==Track listing==\n{{tracklist\n| headline        = \n| all_writing     = [[Faderhead]]\n| title1  = Obnoxiated\n| length1 = 2:08\n| title2  = Escape From the Machine\n| length2 = 4:41\n| title3  = Hot Bath And A Cold Razor\n| length3 = 3:40\n| title4  = The Moth And the Fire\n| length4 = 3:58\n| title5  = Baby Firefly\n| length5 = 3:35\n| title6  = Destroy Improve Rebuild\n| length6 = 4:27\n| title7  = Aim to Misbehave\n| length7 = 2:33\n| title8  = Pussy Rules\n| note8 = feat. Shaolyn\n| length8 = 3:24\n| title9  = The Way to Fuck God\n| length9 = 4:09\n| title10  = Beautiful Freak\n| length10 = 3:39\n| title11  = The Bitch I Love to Hate\n| note11 = feat. Chris Pohl of [[Blutengel]]/[[Terminal Choice]]\n| length11 = 2:37\n| title12  = Do You Know Who I Think I Am?\n| note12 = feat. Ted Phelps of [[Imperative Reaction]]\n| length12 = 3:17\n| title13  = Scumfucker\n| length13 = 4:28\n| title14  = Corpus Crisis\n| length14 = 2:46\n| title15  = Crashkid\n| length15 = 4:48\n| title16  = Regaining Unconsciousness\n| length16 = 1:36\n}}\n\n==Credits==\n* Written, produced, recorded, & mixed by [[Faderhead]]\n* All lyrics by [[Faderhead]]\n*Mastered by James Meeker\n\n==References==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n==External links==\n*[https://web.archive.org/web/20101111050729/http://nxlive.co.uk:80/nxmag/2010/10/interview-faderhead/ Interview with Faderhead at NXLive.co.uk]\n{{Faderhead}}\n[[Category:2010 albums]]\n[[Category:Faderhead albums]]\n{{
-electronic-album-stub}}</text>\n      <sha1>6c14v1j10pcuvrtxp98us37akek083r</sha1>\n    </revision>\n  </page>\n  <page>\n    <title>Category:London Scottis
