[[Botsomtwe\n| Region   = [[Ashanti Region]]\n| MP       = Simon Osei Mensah\n| Party    = [[New Patriotic Party]]\n}}\n\n\u0022'Bosomtwe\u0022' is one of the [[constituency|constituencies]] represented in the [[Parliament of Ghana]]. It elects one [[Member of Parliament|Member of Parliament (MP)]] by the [[first past the post]] system of election. Bosomtwe is located in the [[Botsomtwe Districtof the ]]Ashanti Region]] of [[Ghana]].\n\n==Boundaries==\nThe seat is located within the Botsomtwe District of the Ashanti Region of Ghana.\n\n== Members of Parliament ==\n\n{| class=\u0022wikitable\u0022\n|-\n!Election!!Member!!Party\n|-\n| [[Ghanaian parliamentary election, 1992|1992]]\n| Yaw Addai Boadu\n| [[Every Ghanaian Living Everywhere|EGLE]]\n|-\n| [[Ghanaian parliamentary election, 1996|1996]]\n| Poku Adu-Gyamfi\n| [[New Patriotic Party]]\n|-\n| [[Ghanaian parliamentary election, 2004|2004]]\n| Simon Osei Mensah\n| New Patriotic Party\n|-\n|}\n\n==Elections==\n\n{{Election box begin | title=[[Ghanaian parliamentary election, 2008]]: Bosomtwe\n {{small|1=\u0022Source: [http://www.ghanaweb.com/GhanaHomePage/election2008/parliament.constituency.php?ID=122 Ghana Home Page]\u0022}}}}\n {{Election box candidate\n| party      = [[New Patriotic Party]]\n| candidate  = Simon Osei Mensah\n| votes      = 25,988\n| percentage = 69.9\n| change     = —\n}}\n {{Election box candidate\n| party      = [[National Democratic Congress (Ghana)|National Democratic Congress]]\n| candidate  = [[Joe Oteng-Adjei|Joseph Oteng Adjei]]\n| votes      = 10,293\n| percentage = 27.7\n| change     = —\n}}\n {{Election box candidate\n| party      = [[People's National Convention (Ghana)|People's National Convention]]\n| candidate  = Suleiman Mohammed\n| votes      = 543\n| percentage = 1.5\n| change     = —\n}}\n {{Election box candidate\n| party      = [[convention People's Party]]\n| candidate  = Gilbert Adler Alhassan\n| votes      = 370\n| percentage = 1.0\n| change     = —\n}}\n {{Election box majority\n| votes      = 15,695\n| percentage = 42.2\n| change     = —\n}}\n {{Election box turnout\n| votes      =\n| percentage =\n| change     =\n}}\n{{Election box end}}\n\n==See also==\n*[[List of Ghana Parliament constituencies]]\n\n== References ==\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Constituencies in Ashanti Region of Ghana}}\n\n{{coord missing|Ghana}}\n\n{{DEFAULTSORT:Bosomtwe}}\n[[Category:Parliamentary constituencies in the Ashanti Region]]</text>\n      <sha1>bvx8pdfibvnc6tz2o
